Source: pg-stat-conn
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Dickson S. Guedes <guedes@guedesoft.net>
Standards-Version: 4.7.4
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 postgresql-server-dev-all,
Homepage: https://github.com/guedes/pg_stat_conn
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/guedes/pg_stat_conn
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/guedes/pg_stat_conn.git

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-stat-conn
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${postgresql:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Breaks:
 ${postgresql:Breaks},
Description: per (database, user) connection/disconnection statistics
 pg_stat_conn tracks the cumulative, real-time volume of connections,
 disconnections, and authentication failures isolated per (database, user)
 pair, exposing historical data and allowing granular counter resets in the
 same spirit as pg_stat_statements.
